{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506","id":1585009031,"node_id":"I_kwDOCA8Bec5eeVGH","number":4506,"title":"Sympy fails to import in rustpython","user":{"login":"jimmiebtlr","id":1325560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjU1NjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1325560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr","html_url":"https://github.com/jimmiebtlr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmiebtlr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":947386063,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NDczODYwNjM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/labels/C-bug","name":"C-bug","color":"f5f1fd","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1397253490,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzk3MjUzNDkw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/labels/C-compat","name":"C-compat","color":"f5f1fd","default":false,"description":"A discrepancy between RustPython and CPython","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2023-02-15T00:06:47Z","updated_at":"2024-04-24T04:03:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Feature\r\n\r\n<!-- What Python feature is missing from RustPython? Give a short description of the feature and how you ran into its absence. -->\r\nI'm unsure what feature specifically, but install and import of sympy results in an error that doesn't happen in python.\r\n\r\n```\r\n~ % rustpython -m pip install sympy                                                                                                                           \r\nDefaulting to user installation because normal site-packages is not writeable                                                                                                            \r\nRequirement already satisfied: sympy in ./.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages (1.11.1)                                                                                               \r\nRequirement already satisfied: mpmath>=0.19 in ./.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages (from sympy) (1.2.1)                                                                            \r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n~ % rustpython                                                                                                                                                \r\nWelcome to the magnificent Rust Python 0.2.0 interpreter 😱 🖖  \r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen in the interpreter, running `import sympy` I get the following error.\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):                                                                                                                                                       \r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>                                                                                                                                                    \r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/__init__.py\", line 73, in <module>                                                                                   \r\n    from .polys import (Poly, PurePoly, poly_from_expr, parallel_poly_from_expr,                                                                                                         \r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/polys/__init__.py\", line 75, in <module>                                                                             \r\n    from .polyfuncs import (symmetrize, horner, interpolate,                                                                                                                             \r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/polys/polyfuncs.py\", line 11, in <module>                                                                            \r\n    from sympy.polys.specialpolys import (                                                                                                                                               \r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/polys/specialpolys.py\", line 297, in <module>\r\n    from sympy.polys.rings import ring\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/polys/rings.py\", line 30, in <module>\r\n    from sympy.printing.defaults import DefaultPrinting\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/printing/__init__.py\", line 5, in <module>\r\n    from .latex import latex, print_latex, multiline_latex\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/printing/latex.py\", line 18, in <module>\r\n    from sympy.tensor.array import NDimArray\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/tensor/__init__.py\", line 4, in <module>\r\n    from .indexed import IndexedBase, Idx, Indexed\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/tensor/indexed.py\", line 114, in <module>\r\n    from sympy.functions.special.tensor_functions import KroneckerDelta\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/functions/__init__.py\", line 10, in <module>\r\n    from sympy.functions.combinatorial.numbers import (carmichael, fibonacci, lucas, tribonacci,\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/functions/combinatorial/numbers.py\", line 329, in <module>\r\n    class tribonacci(Function):\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/functions/combinatorial/numbers.py\", line 374, in tribonacci\r\n    @recurrence_memo([S.Zero, S.One, _sym**2]) \r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/expr.py\", line 232, in __pow__\r\n    return self._pow(other)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/decorators.py\", line 236, in _func\r\n    return func(self, other)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/decorators.py\", line 106, in binary_op_wrapper\r\n    return func(self, other)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/expr.py\", line 228, in _pow\r\n    return Pow(self, other)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/cache.py\", line 74, in wrapper\r\n    retval = func(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/cache.py\", line 70, in wrapper\r\n    retval = cfunc(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.cargo/git/checkouts/rustpython-f8ef4d934ac33cd8/adc2325/pylib/Lib/functools.py\", line 593, in wrapper\r\n    result = user_function(*args, **kwds)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/power.py\", line 355, in __new__\r\n    from sympy.functions.elementary.exponential import exp_polar\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/functions/elementary/exponential.py\", line 1124, in <module>\r\n    class LambertW(Function):\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/functions/elementary/exponential.py\", line 1159, in LambertW\r\n    _singularities = (-Pow(S.Exp1, -1, evaluate=False), S.ComplexInfinity)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/cache.py\", line 74, in wrapper\r\n    retval = func(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/cache.py\", line 70, in wrapper\r\n    retval = cfunc(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.cargo/git/checkouts/rustpython-f8ef4d934ac33cd8/adc2325/pylib/Lib/functools.py\", line 593, in wrapper\r\n    result = user_function(*args, **kwds)\r\n  File \"<reported-home>/.local/lib/rustpython3.10/site-packages/sympy/core/power.py\", line 378, in __new__\r\n    obj.is_commutative = (b.is_commutative and e.is_commutative)\r\nAttributeError: can't set attribute\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Python Documentation\r\n\r\n<!-- Give a link to the feature in the CPython documentation (https://docs.python.org/3/) in order to assist in its implementation. -->\r\n\r\nSympy docs are here\r\nhttps://www.sympy.org/en/index.html","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4506/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}